A||||1||deceler8||Auto trans boot..."collar" at top...||||1||
Z||000000||deceler8||11-10-2001||09:54 AM||||If you've got an auto trans Fiero and the thing that covers up the seams at the top of the shift boot is missing...look in your medicine cabinet.<P>I discovered the cap from a bottle of cough syrup works if you drill a 1/2 inch hole in the center and drop it down over the top of the boot.<P>Any cap with an outside diameter of an inch or so will work, and a lot of medicine bottle caps are black, so check out your medicine cabinet.<P>Don't know why this occurred to me the other day, but I hope it helps some of you.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mickey_Moose||11-10-2001||11:53 AM||||I just made a different boot that has a wider opening at the top so that the boot comes all the way up to the bottom of the shift handle (rolled the top of the boot down inside).  The original boot I thought looked goofy being so short when it ended at the bottom of the handle.<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||6
